1.3932.073Similarly, Section 2.2 of Szunerits describes a variety of methods for fabricating metal nanostructures on a surface, and pictures of such surfaces containing metal nanostructures are shown in Figs. 3 and 4. Such surfaces are usually substantially transparent, as this is necessary in order to determine the refraction index-see, e.g., the Abstract of Szunerits, which explains that measuring changes in the local refractive index is needed for localized surface plasmon resonance.

