1.125.083Nowhere is it seen where Szunerits teaches or suggests that the particles can be attached to the end portion of a member, i.e., such that the at least one particle is positioned in an optically interrogatable position with respect to the member (where the light is transmitted therethrough), as is recited in claim 1. For example, Szunerits nowhere teaches or suggests immobilizing the particles onto a light source rather than the surface of a sample. Instead, Szunerits teaches that in surface plasma resonance, the particle should be immobilized onto a transparent surface, such that changes in the local refractive index can be determined.
